    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDerelict Farmhouse on c. 45.6 acres of Lands\n\nThe lands of 18.46 hectares are contained in Folio LD11710. \nThe lands are divided by a road and have a combined road frontage of c. 1,136 meters onto a narrow country road. Therefore there may be an opportunity to get planning for a single dwelling site at some point in the future.\n\nIn addition there is a derelict farm house and old stone outbuildings that could take advantage of the vacant property grants which offers grants up to 70,000 for derelict properties.\nThe lands are of good quality divided out into large fields. We would estimate that c. 31.3 acres of the grounds are of this quality. These lands have been actively farmed and the boundaries and hedges are in good condition and well maintained.\n\nThe remaining lands are poorer quality and cutaway bog area. \nThe lands are situated just off the R392 Ballymahon Lanesboro road on the south of County Longford. The area is beside the Corlea trackway bog walk and amenity area. 8km North west of Ballymahon, 11km South east of Lanesboro and less than 5 km from Kenagh Village.\n\n\nDirections \nGPS: 53.6417, -7.7510"
      },
